          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The characteristics of the observation (orange 'fireball' with several peaks inside (combustible flames), stationary or moving slowly, abruptly going out (end of combustible), time of observation (Saturday night around midnight...)) strongly evoke the characteristics of a flying lantern observation. The observation has a low degree of strangeness. The case consistency remains low (one witness reporting through an official statement and questionnaire for 5 witnesses), with the other witnesses not testifying directly. The phenomenon's location is quite precise, allowing for a release at high altitudes facing the observation site (existing road). The case is classified as B, indicating a probable observation of a Thai lantern.",
